= Consciousness (simple) =

'''Consciousness''' often means having experiences: seeing colors, feeling pain, or being aware of something. Scientists also study related abilities such as noticing information, reporting it, and using it to make decisions. Those abilities are not exactly the same thing as having an inner experience.

Researchers study the brain and behavior, including what changes during sleep and anesthesia. Several theories explain the findings differently. No single theory has been conclusively established.

A computer, robot, or AI agent can process information and report on its own state. That behavior alone does not prove that it has feelings or subjective experiences; nor does it resolve the broader scientific question.

